# Separate compilation where a dependency is reached only through another
# module.
#
# 13_separate imports both `shapes` and `square`, and lists `shapes` first, so
# the order the driver produced happened to be right and a real bug in it went
# unseen: modules were recorded *before* their own imports, so a program
# importing only `square` got the order "square shapes" and compiled `square`
# before `shapes` existed to import. The build failed with
# "Type 'Shape' not found in Type Table."
#
# This file imports only `square`. `shapes` has to be found, ordered and
# compiled first on its own account.

using square

class Main from IO
  def main:
    Square s
    s.report()
    out("area ${s.area()}\n")
  end
end
